From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 04:02:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/35] media: mediatek: seninf: RAW engines as a second
 destination of a CSI port

An output port can now carry a second endpoint to a node with
mediatek,raw-id. Such a port gets a third pad for it and a static route
through its own mux of the RAW range (6..8), the first virtual mux of that
mux (0x22..0x2d) and the cam mux of the engine (0x22 RAW-A, 0x24 RAW-B). A
port without a RAW endpoint keeps its two pads and its graph.

One destination of a port streams at a time: the route is claimed when
the stream is enabled, before the receiver and the sensor start, and a
mux held by another running port is -EBUSY with the holder named. A RAW
destination filters by virtual channel and data type in the cam mux
option register only (no tags). A RAW engine driver without a media graph
of its own finds its CSI port sub-device and source pad through its
endpoint.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
